<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9781" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάνειρᾰ</span></b> , ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί, ἀνήρ</span>), fem. form of a masc. in
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άνωρ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήνωρ</span>: in <i><span class="en">
			Il.
		</span></i> always as epith. of the Amazons, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a match for men,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				3.189
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.186
			</span></i>, etc.; so of Athena, <i><span class="en">
				Coluth.
				170
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				12.16
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάσις ἀντιάνειρα</span> faction
				<i>wherein man is set against man.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
